hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1149","Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani and Ali bin Al-Mundhir told us, they said: Ibn Fudayl told us, Ali said, he said: Husayn told us, and he said Harun, on the authority of Husayn, H. Abu Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abtar narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Hudhayfah He said: “Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up at night to pray Tahajjud, he would garnish his mouth with the siwak.” Aaron and Abu Husayn said: When he stands, he performs Hajj."
